<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  日本語 — PARTIALLY REVIEWED. 2026-08-27: a native speaker returned 121 of 339
  strings — 108 rewritten, 13 approved as they stood. Those are in. The
  remaining 214 are still the unreviewed first pass and are NOT idiomatic by
  default (i18n spec §9: plausible and consistent is not the same as
  idiomatic). Status per key lives in docs/l10n-review-ja.csv.

  ⚠️ FOUR REVIEWED STRINGS WERE HELD BACK, and each was a defect rather than a
  preference — see the 2026-08-27 commit:
    ago_day/ago_hr/ago_min  a stray full-width 1 ("%1$d１日前" renders "3 1日前")
    al_lookalike            no such key in values/strings.xml
  and one was corrected on the way in:
    f_erase_arm             洗濯 (laundry) -> 選択 (select). Same reading,
                            せんたく; the English is "PICK AGAIN TO ERASE".

  Conventions held throughout:

  - Protocol tokens stay Latin: B, COMMIT, HERE, GPS, ON — they name gestures,
    controls and pips whose marks are Latin, and a control's spoken name must
    match its printed one.
  - Terse over polite: this is an instrument register, so 未接続 rather than
    接続されていません. It also buys width — kanji costs 1.5x the cap and 2
    cells a glyph (see L10n).
  - Half-width digits and %-args everywhere; counts read better beside Latin
    units and callsigns, which never translate.
-->
